DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ppccaapp__ccaann__sseett__rrffmmoonn() checks whether monitor mode could be set on a cap‐
       ture handle when the handle is activated.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       ppccaapp__ccaann__sseett__rrffmmoonn()  returns  00 if monitor mode could not be set, 11 if
       monitor mode could be set, and a negative value on error.   A  negative
       return value indicates what error condition occurred.  The possible er‐
       ror values are:

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__NNOO__SSUUCCHH__DDEEVVIICCEE
              The capture source specified when the handle was created doesn't
              exist.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__PPEERRMM__DDEENNIIEEDD
              The  process  doesn't  have  permission to check whether monitor
              mode could be supported.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__AACCTTIIVVAATTEEDD
              The capture handle has already been activated.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR
              Another error occurred.  ppccaapp__ggeetteerrrr(3) or ppccaapp__ppeerrrroorr(3) may be
              called  with  _p as an argument to fetch or display a message de‐
              scribing the error.

       Additional error codes may be added in the  future;  a  program  should
       check  for 00, 11, and negative, return codes, and treat all negative re‐
       turn codes as errors.  ppccaapp__ssttaattuussttoossttrr(3) can be called, with a  warn‐
       ing  or  error  code  as an argument, to fetch a message describing the
       warning or error code.

